  "notes": "Compound of {養|よう} (to raise/keep) + {蜂|ほう} (bee). The standard term for beekeeping.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {養蜂|ようほう}{家|か}: beekeeper\n- {養蜂|ようほう}{場|じょう}: apiary, bee farm\n- {養蜂|ようほう}{箱|ばこ}: beehive box\n- {養蜂|ようほう}を{始|はじ}める: to start beekeeping\n\nRELATED {養|よう}～ COMPOUNDS:\n- {養殖|ようしょく}: aquaculture (raising fish/shellfish)\n- {養鶏|ようけい}: poultry farming\n- {養豚|ようとん}: pig farming\n\nCULTURAL NOTE:\nUrban beekeeping ({都市|とし}{養蜂|ようほう}) on rooftops has become popular, especially in {東京|とうきょう} and {大阪|おおさか}. Japanese honeybees ({日本|にほん}ミツバチ) are distinct from Western honeybees ({西洋|せいよう}ミツバチ).",
